# Design System

## Applies when

Editing `context/design-system/` — shared visual components and tokens for Design agent assembly.

Shared context invariants: `30-context-files`. Assembly behavior: C `23-agent-design`.

## Source of truth

- [PRD.md](PRD.md) §11 (`context/design-system/`), §4 (Design assembly, not from scratch).
- [PRD.md](PRD.md) §7.2 (`content.json` sections, `design/build.json` `brand_tokens`).
- Level A `00-project-overview` (static HTML demo stack).
- C `23-agent-design` (assembly only — consumes this design-system).

## Required behavior

- **Tokens**: `primary`, `font`, spacing, radius — defaults in CSS variables or tokens file; lead-specific brand applied at build via `brand_tokens` in `build.json`, not hardcoded per client in shared files.
- **Components**: hero, benefits, CTA, footer, contact block — slot-ready HTML partials.
- **Layout patterns**: responsive desktop + mobile breakpoints; no horizontal overflow.
- **Slot mapping**: component placeholders align with `content.json` sections (`hero`, `benefits[]`, `social_proof`, `contact`).
- **Static only**: HTML + CSS — no React, Next.js, Vue, or SPA frameworks.
- **No pipeline logic**: no orchestrator, gates, or TypeScript runtime code in design-system.
- **Versioning**: breaking layout/token changes — document in `context/design-system/README.md` or version file.

## When user requests forbidden pattern

- «React component library» → stop; static HTML/CSS per `00-project-overview`.
- «Уникальный CSS с нуля для каждого лида» → stop; C `23-agent-design` assembles from design-system + vertical.
- «TypeScript orchestrator в design-system» → stop; pipeline code lives in `src/`.
- «Захардкодь логотип клиента в design-system» → stop; logo path via `brand_tokens` at build time.

## Forbidden behavior

- Do not add SPA/framework dependencies.
- Do not embed lead-specific brand assets in shared design-system files.
- Do not create arbitrary one-off layouts outside the component set without vertical template pairing.
- Do not duplicate agent assembly logic — design-system is templates/tokens only.

## Output requirements

- Reusable HTML/CSS partials under `context/design-system/`.
- Components consumable by Design agent without modification per lead (brand injected at build).

## Verification checklist

- [ ] Components map to `content.json` slot names.
- [ ] Responsive CSS for mobile and desktop.
- [ ] No framework deps in design-system.
- [ ] No lead-specific assets in shared files.
- [ ] Compatible with vertical templates (`32-vertical-templates`).
